cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Axion or its evaluation benchmark in academic work, please cite this repository."
title: "Axion: A Claim-Level Knowledge Graph for Contradiction-First Literature Review"
abstract: >-
  Axion turns a corpus of research papers into an inspectable graph of atomic
  claims, supporting evidence, contradictions, and open questions. It extracts
  claims with section-level provenance, stores them in Neo4j and ChromaDB,
  adjudicates cross-paper relationships with an LLM, and derives research gaps,
  resolving experiments, temporal consensus, and citation-weighted confidence.
  The repository includes a human-audited claim-pair benchmark and a
  pre-registered judge ablation.
type: software
authors:
